            "type": "game",
            "name": "Jung's Labyrinth",
            "steam_appid": 709710,
            "required_age": "14",
            "is_free": false,
            "detailed_description": "<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/709710/extras/be317290f09181e5f498bb23fe9a5b13.avif?t=1726765100\" width=600 height=77 /></span><br>Based on teachings of Carl G. Jung, this game explores the themes of so called Individuation process and active imagination - the game allows you to talk with your inner archetypes and leads you on the road to your true Self.<br><br>The game's progress is based on the classic hero journey, where you have to confront your Ego archetypes, notice your Shadow projections; integrate your Shadow; work with your Soul archetypes; integrate your Anima and Senex; and only then you will be allowed to progress to your Self.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/709710/extras/298ebb00e4f6bd15246a16e1e81d7104.avif?t=1726765100\" width=600 height=77 /></span><br>You can play in VR by switching to the beta branch virtual_reality and restarting the Steam client after installing the game. Only Oculus Rift S supported.<br><br>More information about VR support: <br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/709710/extras/a6797e442713551f82cc83fdb9789e92.avif?t=1726765100\" width=600 height=77 /></span><br>Linux is also supported, but only on an untested beta branch. <br><br>More information on Linux version: ",
            "about_the_game": "<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/709710/extras/be317290f09181e5f498bb23fe9a5b13.avif?t=1726765100\" width=600 height=77 /></span><br>Based on teachings of Carl G. Jung, this game explores the themes of so called Individuation process and active imagination - the game allows you to talk with your inner archetypes and leads you on the road to your true Self.<br><br>The game's progress is based on the classic hero journey, where you have to confront your Ego archetypes, notice your Shadow projections; integrate your Shadow; work with your Soul archetypes; integrate your Anima and Senex; and only then you will be allowed to progress to your Self.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/709710/extras/298ebb00e4f6bd15246a16e1e81d7104.avif?t=1726765100\" width=600 height=77 /></span><br>You can play in VR by switching to the beta branch virtual_reality and restarting the Steam client after installing the game. Only Oculus Rift S supported.<br><br>More information about VR support: <br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/709710/extras/a6797e442713551f82cc83fdb9789e92.avif?t=1726765100\" width=600 height=77 /></span><br>Linux is also supported, but only on an untested beta branch. <br><br>More information on Linux version: ",
            "short_description": "Jung's Labyrinth is a psychological exploration game that uses Jungian psychology, mythology, alchemical and dream symbolism in a series of active imaginations to map the process of individuation. Confront your inner archetypes, collect messages that other travelers left behind and reach your Self.",
            "supported_languages": "Inglês<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>idiomas com suporte total de áudio",
            "reviews": {
                "query_summary": {
                    "num_reviews": 1,
                    "review_score": 6,
                    "review_score_desc": "Mostly Positive",
                    "total_positive": 49,
                    "total_negative": 18,
                    "total_reviews": 67
                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "236917892",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199050699598",
                            "num_reviews": 16,
                            "playtime_forever": 422,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 422,
                            "last_played": 1777407731
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As the price is lower now I'd rather recommend you this journey for just a few hours. The labyrinths themselves are quite tricky and easy to get lost in, so be prepared for a little bit demanding trip, rather than a relaxing one. I am kinda confused in the way a game shows confronting your shadows, cuz them are shown as a cockroaches following and trying to hurt you, at the moment you are searching for archetypes in the labyrinth then collecting philosophical stones. Kinda weird, that it's not a huge concept to contemplate. In this interpretation the process of the integration is just talking to your inner selfs, sometimes the ones you don't even want to acknowledge. Doing it and taming them gives you some sort of power.....maybe?",
